1
00:00:01,721 --> 00:00:04,140
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:01:31,101 --> 00:01:35,731
BLOOD IN THE DISCO BALL

3
00:01:36,315 --> 00:01:37,942
[news anchor] <i>It's been nearly two weeks</i>

4
00:01:38,025 --> 00:01:40,152
{\an8}<i>since the gray wolf Legoshi,
has been on the run.</i>

5
00:01:40,236 --> 00:01:42,988
<i>First question on my mind is.
what are the police doing?</i>

6
00:01:43,072 --> 00:01:44,490
<i>Well, clearly they're slacking.</i>

7
00:01:44,573 --> 00:01:47,535
<i>I mean, come on, if they still
can't find him, that tells me</i>

8
00:01:47,618 --> 00:01:50,830
<i>he's gotta be hiding somewhere
in the black market. Right?</i>

9
00:01:50,913 --> 00:01:52,957
<i>Yeah, yeah, yeah. That does makes sense.</i>

10
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:54,834
<i>If I were a criminal, I'd hide myself</i>

11
00:01:54,917 --> 00:01:57,169
<i>in a place that police
wouldn't be able to search.</i>

12
00:01:57,253 --> 00:01:58,921
<i>That might be one of the reasons</i>

13
00:01:59,004 --> 00:02:01,382
<i>the police announced they'll pay
ten million Yen</i>

14
00:02:01,465 --> 00:02:04,426
<i>to anyone who can provide information
leading to his arrest.</i>

15
00:02:04,510 --> 00:02:06,679
<i>That's the highest reward
in our history, isn't it?</i>

16
00:02:06,762 --> 00:02:10,641
<i>Absolutely. But if he did commit more
than 20 violent crimes...</i>

17
00:02:10,724 --> 00:02:12,935
He was at the restaurant six days a week.

18
00:02:13,018 --> 00:02:14,937
Twenty crimes seems impossible.

19
00:02:15,729 --> 00:02:17,148
<i>Forget about the Zoolympics,</i>

20
00:02:17,231 --> 00:02:21,402
<i>isn't more important to make sure
our citizens are safe first and foremost?</i>

21
00:02:21,485 --> 00:02:24,613
- [anchors continues]
- [phone line ringing]

22
00:02:24,697 --> 00:02:25,865
Yeah, it's the Mayor.

23
00:02:26,407 --> 00:02:29,076
Turns out that gray wolf is going to
show up tomorrow

24
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:31,036
at the Black Market turf war.

25
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,997
Capture him, no matter what.

26
00:02:33,998 --> 00:02:34,915
{\an8}Right.

27
00:02:35,708 --> 00:02:37,585
{\an8}Up to you, dead or alive.

28
00:02:38,752 --> 00:02:40,671
{\an8}How could he?! [groans]

29
00:02:40,754 --> 00:02:41,714
{\an8}[whimpers]

30
00:02:42,464 --> 00:02:45,926
{\an8}It was obvious he only ever cared about
power and profit...

31
00:02:46,719 --> 00:02:50,639
{\an8}but I never expected my father
to try and get there through bribery.

32
00:02:50,723 --> 00:02:53,726
{\an8}He's as twisted as the horns on his head!
I can't stand it!

33
00:02:53,809 --> 00:02:55,477
{\an8}- [breathing heavily]
- Louis, sir...

34
00:02:55,561 --> 00:02:57,146
You gonna tell me to stay quiet too?

35
00:02:57,938 --> 00:02:59,356
[groans] Not at all...

36
00:02:59,899 --> 00:03:01,483
[cellphone vibrating]

37
00:03:03,193 --> 00:03:04,361
[sighs]

38
00:03:04,445 --> 00:03:05,321
{\an8}Hey, Chloe.

39
00:03:05,404 --> 00:03:07,865
{\an8}[Chlo] <i>I found it.
Exactly what you wanted.</i>

40
00:03:08,532 --> 00:03:10,618
{\an8}<i>-It's here, but...</i>
- Fantastic. That's great to hear.

41
00:03:10,701 --> 00:03:13,704
{\an8}How about I stop by and see you tomorrow?
We'll chat about this then.

42
00:03:13,787 --> 00:03:15,789
{\an8}[Chloe sighs] <i>Unbelievable!</i>

43
00:03:15,873 --> 00:03:18,083
{\an8}<i>-Just like your father...</i>
- What?

44
00:03:18,167 --> 00:03:20,419
{\an8}- Did my father do something?
<i>- Tomorrow, then!</i>

45
00:03:20,502 --> 00:03:21,962
{\an8}[line disconnects]

46
00:03:22,713 --> 00:03:24,006
[sighs in exasperation]

47
00:03:28,594 --> 00:03:30,971
I'm sorry. That was uncalled for.

48
00:03:31,055 --> 00:03:32,556
Forgive me, sir.

49
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:35,643
You should know
this isn't what your father really wants.

50
00:03:35,726 --> 00:03:38,145
Unfortunately, he's being threatened.

51
00:03:38,229 --> 00:03:39,605
Wait, what are you saying?

52
00:03:40,147 --> 00:03:44,652
Apparently, the mayor did some digging
through your past with your father.

53
00:03:44,735 --> 00:03:47,029
I hear he found something
rather troubling.

54
00:03:47,905 --> 00:03:49,865
[sighs in surprise]
<i>The Black Market catalogue?</i>

55
00:03:49,949 --> 00:03:51,825
<i>He swore to me he'd throw that away.</i>

56
00:03:52,576 --> 00:03:55,454
It's important you understand
your father's actions.

57
00:03:55,955 --> 00:03:58,499
I assure you, he wanted no part of this.

58
00:03:59,166 --> 00:04:00,584
Well, thank you for that.

59
00:04:00,668 --> 00:04:03,379
If this part of my past got out,
it'd stain the foundation.

60
00:04:03,462 --> 00:04:04,880
You're not understanding.

61
00:04:05,381 --> 00:04:06,632
It's about you.

62
00:04:06,715 --> 00:04:08,926
Your father is worried about you, Louis.

63
00:04:09,426 --> 00:04:10,427
About me?

64
00:04:10,511 --> 00:04:11,345
Yes.

65
00:04:11,929 --> 00:04:15,266
He won't stand by
and allow your future to be destroyed.

66
00:04:17,101 --> 00:04:18,560
<i>He actually cares?</i>

67
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:32,408
[Jimma breathing heavily]

68
00:04:38,455 --> 00:04:39,957
Look at all that meat!

69
00:04:41,041 --> 00:04:42,543
I know, dammit!

70
00:04:44,128 --> 00:04:45,879
[groans] I can't take it anymore!

71
00:04:45,963 --> 00:04:47,047
Calm down!

72
00:04:49,091 --> 00:04:51,719
Here, why dontcha chew on Louis' antler?

73
00:05:00,728 --> 00:05:03,355
It's on me.
Didn't mean to keep you waiting.

74
00:05:03,439 --> 00:05:05,524
I'm surprised you're able to show up
on time

75
00:05:05,607 --> 00:05:07,234
for anything riding that junk heap.

76
00:05:07,318 --> 00:05:09,320
She's still got plenty of miles in her.

77
00:05:10,029 --> 00:05:11,739
Tell me what it is we're doing here.

78
00:05:12,281 --> 00:05:15,034
I can only assume
since you went out of your way...

79
00:05:15,117 --> 00:05:17,286
I take it it's about your grandson.

80
00:05:17,369 --> 00:05:19,788
[grunts softly] Well, you've still got it.

81
00:05:19,872 --> 00:05:20,914
[paper rustling]

82
00:05:20,998 --> 00:05:23,625
This letter right here is from Legoshi.

83
00:05:23,709 --> 00:05:24,752
So uh...

84
00:05:26,712 --> 00:05:28,505
"I hope things are going well.

85
00:05:28,589 --> 00:05:32,092
I wanted to talk to you in person,
but that's not possible at the moment.

86
00:05:33,135 --> 00:05:36,138
I appreciate you
continuing to take care of Haru.

87
00:05:36,638 --> 00:05:39,183
But remember to take care of yourself,
while you're at it.

88
00:05:39,266 --> 00:05:40,350
Legoshi."

89
00:05:40,434 --> 00:05:43,187
It was The Five Hundred Cornered Rats
who delivered it.

90
00:05:43,270 --> 00:05:45,147
Aren't those little critters your friends?

91
00:05:45,230 --> 00:05:46,899
Maybe those rodents know something?

92
00:05:46,982 --> 00:05:50,152
What do you think's behind this letter?
Suicide note?

93
00:05:50,235 --> 00:05:51,236
[grunts softly]

94
00:05:52,196 --> 00:05:53,739
{\an8}I'm definitely worried about him.

95
00:05:53,822 --> 00:05:56,241
{\an8}I hope he's not planning anything crazy.

96
00:05:56,325 --> 00:05:59,495
{\an8}If Legoshi makes a move
he'll fall right into our net.

97
00:05:59,578 --> 00:06:02,289
Huh? Ya wanna let me in on the plan here?

98
00:06:02,372 --> 00:06:04,792
Well, he's a wanted criminal.
We'll arrest him.

99
00:06:04,875 --> 00:06:06,919
- I appreciate you providing information.
- Hang on!

100
00:06:07,002 --> 00:06:08,837
You know he didn't do a damn thing!

101
00:06:08,921 --> 00:06:11,423
- Alright, Corne, its time.
- Hey, what are you doin', Yahya?!

102
00:06:11,507 --> 00:06:12,925
Looks like he's making a move.

103
00:06:13,008 --> 00:06:14,927
He's aiming for the Black Market.

104
00:06:15,010 --> 00:06:17,054
- Issue the orders.
- You dirty slime bag!

105
00:06:17,137 --> 00:06:19,348
I was an idiot thinking I could trust you!

106
00:06:28,357 --> 00:06:31,026
<i>You never change, do you, old friend?</i>

107
00:06:31,110 --> 00:06:32,277
<i>What a shame.</i>

108
00:06:33,904 --> 00:06:38,951
[Melon laughing]

109
00:06:43,747 --> 00:06:48,752
[Giant legoshi growling]

110
00:06:53,298 --> 00:06:55,384
[both growling]

111
00:07:01,223 --> 00:07:02,224
[gasps]

112
00:07:06,061 --> 00:07:07,521
- [sighs]
- [heavy breathing]

113
00:07:14,194 --> 00:07:15,028
[sighs]

114
00:07:16,363 --> 00:07:18,490
- [metal clinging]
- [groans]

115
00:07:23,162 --> 00:07:26,665
<i>The leopard in me
grows and the gazelle retreats...</i>

116
00:07:29,418 --> 00:07:32,004
Oh Melon, you seem lost in thought.

117
00:07:33,505 --> 00:07:35,174
[Melon] <i>Just the two of us,</i>

118
00:07:35,257 --> 00:07:37,342
<i>in the strange fairy-tale world</i>

119
00:07:37,426 --> 00:07:40,262
<i>mother made for us
to escape from real life...</i>

120
00:07:41,054 --> 00:07:43,223
<i>Living in make believe.</i>

121
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,059
Melon, my darling...

122
00:07:46,143 --> 00:07:48,562
[Melon] <i>I loved just hearing mom
say my name.</i>

123
00:07:49,605 --> 00:07:53,442
<i>In those moments
I wasn't a carnivore or an herbivore...</i>

124
00:07:54,276 --> 00:07:57,362
<i>I was just myself... just Melon.</i>

125
00:07:58,113 --> 00:08:02,367
[mother] Your timid little face...
and that frail body of yours.

126
00:08:02,910 --> 00:08:05,621
You remind me so much of your daddy.

127
00:08:06,205 --> 00:08:08,916
I just adored
everything about that gazelle.

128
00:08:10,125 --> 00:08:12,794
[licks lips]

129
00:08:12,878 --> 00:08:14,046
[sighs]

130
00:08:14,129 --> 00:08:17,758
<i>She was my everything...
her terrifying beauty...</i>

131
00:08:19,134 --> 00:08:21,512
<i>The gazelle inside of me is disappearing.</i>

132
00:08:22,054 --> 00:08:23,180
[strains]

133
00:08:26,725 --> 00:08:28,727
[Louis] Very impressive facilities.

134
00:08:28,810 --> 00:08:30,062
Even a smoking room.

135
00:08:30,604 --> 00:08:31,480
I suppose.

136
00:08:32,397 --> 00:08:34,608
What happened between you and my father?

137
00:08:35,192 --> 00:08:36,193
[Chloe sighs]

138
00:08:37,027 --> 00:08:38,028
Let me guess.

139
00:08:38,111 --> 00:08:40,197
Something about the artificial meat?

140
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:42,157
Oh, so you know about that?

141
00:08:42,658 --> 00:08:44,326
There was some drama.

142
00:08:44,409 --> 00:08:46,328
When I gave him the lab results, he said:

143
00:08:46,411 --> 00:08:49,915
"This cannot be allowed to stand,
I'll leak it to the media!"

144
00:08:49,998 --> 00:08:51,750
He was really worked up about it.

145
00:08:51,833 --> 00:08:52,834
[scoffs]

146
00:08:52,918 --> 00:08:54,795
<i>What is she talking about?</i>

147
00:08:54,878 --> 00:08:58,006
- So, what exactly did you tell him?
- Only the truth.

148
00:08:58,715 --> 00:09:00,008
The lab results confirmed

149
00:09:00,092 --> 00:09:02,678
the artificial meat wasn't
fully lab-grown,

150
00:09:02,761 --> 00:09:05,430
turns out some of it
is from early stage embryos.

151
00:09:05,931 --> 00:09:07,224
[Louis] <i>That's insane...</i>

152
00:09:07,891 --> 00:09:09,434
But the very next day,

153
00:09:09,518 --> 00:09:12,437
he gave me strict orders
to never speak of it again.

154
00:09:12,521 --> 00:09:14,231
- Well that's suspicious.
- Yeah.

155
00:09:14,815 --> 00:09:17,693
Like someone threatened him into silence.

156
00:09:17,776 --> 00:09:20,571
From what I could tell,
he seemed to be suffering.

157
00:09:20,654 --> 00:09:23,532
[Yuta] <i>You should know
this isn't what your father really wants.</i>

158
00:09:23,615 --> 00:09:25,784
Unfortunately, he's being threatened.

159
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:30,414
Anyway, regarding
the blood coagulation inhibitor drug,

160
00:09:30,998 --> 00:09:33,292
I've got a delivery update for you.

161
00:09:33,375 --> 00:09:34,376
Yes?

162
00:09:34,459 --> 00:09:37,087
Earliest I can get it in your hands
would be two days.

163
00:09:37,170 --> 00:09:39,381
[stutters] Why the delay?

164
00:09:39,464 --> 00:09:41,300
[Chloe] We can't just take anything
we want.

165
00:09:41,383 --> 00:09:42,884
There's an application process.

166
00:09:42,968 --> 00:09:45,679
Two days isn't going to work.
I need it tonight.

167
00:09:45,762 --> 00:09:47,848
- Tonight?
- My friend, uh...

168
00:09:47,931 --> 00:09:49,016
he's fighting a duel.

169
00:09:49,099 --> 00:09:53,228
And what does your friend fighting a duel
have to do with blood clotting?

170
00:09:53,770 --> 00:09:55,314
It has to do with his opponent.

171
00:09:55,397 --> 00:09:57,941
He's the one behind all these
serial devourings.

172
00:09:58,025 --> 00:10:01,320
- What?
- He's a very powerful hybrid.

173
00:10:01,403 --> 00:10:04,698
By mixing herbivore and carnivore blood,
we discovered his weakness.

174
00:10:04,781 --> 00:10:05,907
And we need this edge.

175
00:10:06,575 --> 00:10:08,744
When you mix the blood
of different species,

176
00:10:08,827 --> 00:10:10,329
it clots instantly, right?

177
00:10:11,246 --> 00:10:14,499
I get it now. And I really would
love to be able to help you--

178
00:10:14,583 --> 00:10:16,043
[Louis] I made a promise...

179
00:10:16,126 --> 00:10:17,461
that I would fight too.

180
00:10:17,544 --> 00:10:18,795
Why would you fight?

181
00:10:18,879 --> 00:10:21,465
Because his pain is also my pain.

182
00:10:22,633 --> 00:10:24,843
Every time he has to fight,
he does it alone.

183
00:10:26,094 --> 00:10:28,639
He never hesitates
to put himself in danger.

184
00:10:28,722 --> 00:10:31,058
Especially to protect someone
he cares for.

185
00:10:31,141 --> 00:10:35,062
No matter how lost he gets,
in the end he always faces things head-on.

186
00:10:36,271 --> 00:10:38,774
At the same time, I do the opposite.

187
00:10:38,857 --> 00:10:42,152
I stand there doing nothing
while those I care about get hurt.

188
00:10:43,403 --> 00:10:45,989
You really want to help the guy,
don't you?

189
00:10:46,073 --> 00:10:47,741
It's the right thing to do.

190
00:10:47,824 --> 00:10:51,244
Maybe we're cowards for trying to use
this "blood trick".

191
00:10:51,328 --> 00:10:54,456
Still, sometimes you can't win
by fighting fair.

192
00:10:54,539 --> 00:10:56,249
I think you're in the right.

193
00:10:56,875 --> 00:10:57,959
<i>"In the right..."</i>

194
00:10:58,794 --> 00:10:59,836
[sighs]

195
00:11:00,462 --> 00:11:01,463
<i>But am I though?</i>

196
00:11:02,047 --> 00:11:03,298
[scoffs] <i>No.</i>

197
00:11:04,049 --> 00:11:06,093
<i>Legoshi would never do things this way.</i>

198
00:11:06,802 --> 00:11:08,929
<i>There's no way I can go through with this.</i>

199
00:11:10,806 --> 00:11:11,973
Hold on.

200
00:11:12,057 --> 00:11:14,810
I can't be a coward.
I've got to do this with honor.

201
00:11:14,893 --> 00:11:16,103
[gasps]

202
00:11:16,186 --> 00:11:17,479
That's final.

203
00:11:17,562 --> 00:11:18,522
<i>That's who I am.</i>

204
00:11:19,064 --> 00:11:20,190
<i>It's so clear to me.</i>

205
00:11:20,273 --> 00:11:21,983
<i>I have to fight my own enemy.</i>

206
00:11:22,651 --> 00:11:24,361
<i>Isn't that right, Legoshi?</i>

207
00:11:26,571 --> 00:11:27,739
I appreciate you.

208
00:11:27,823 --> 00:11:29,032
Excuse me.

209
00:11:29,116 --> 00:11:31,201
I know what I have to do. We'll talk soon.

210
00:11:31,785 --> 00:11:33,829
Hey, wait, uh...

211
00:11:33,912 --> 00:11:35,122
Hang on!

212
00:11:37,707 --> 00:11:39,251
[sighs]

213
00:11:39,334 --> 00:11:41,294
Are you sure you're an herbivore?

214
00:11:41,378 --> 00:11:42,754
Your blood's way too hot.

215
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:46,425
{\an8}GIANT PANDA

216
00:11:46,508 --> 00:11:47,717
{\an8}[Legoshi] <i>You're a life saver.</i>

217
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:49,970
You're the only one I could trust.

218
00:11:50,053 --> 00:11:52,055
So thank you for doing this, Mr. Gohin.

219
00:11:52,139 --> 00:11:53,765
Oh, come on.

220
00:11:53,849 --> 00:11:55,851
Didn't you almost get killed twice?

221
00:11:55,934 --> 00:11:57,561
I wonder if you'll ever learn...

222
00:11:57,644 --> 00:12:00,147
Yeah, but, I came back to life both times.

223
00:12:00,230 --> 00:12:01,440
Can't say I get it.

224
00:12:01,523 --> 00:12:04,693
When people fight they normally reach
for weapons and armor.

225
00:12:04,776 --> 00:12:06,278
But you drain your own blood,

226
00:12:06,361 --> 00:12:08,280
and pull out your own fangs.

227
00:12:08,363 --> 00:12:10,699
You'd think you'd wanna be
in your best shape.

228
00:12:10,782 --> 00:12:11,825
Crazy.

229
00:12:11,908 --> 00:12:13,243
In my experience,

230
00:12:13,326 --> 00:12:15,036
I found my best weapons

231
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:18,748
haven't necessarily been the gifts
I was born with as a carnivore.

232
00:12:18,832 --> 00:12:20,584
It's not my traits as a wolf,

233
00:12:20,667 --> 00:12:21,877
these claws and fangs.

234
00:12:22,377 --> 00:12:24,754
It's everything I've experienced and felt.

235
00:12:24,838 --> 00:12:26,423
That's what I lean on.

236
00:12:26,506 --> 00:12:28,091
[sighs]

237
00:12:28,175 --> 00:12:30,677
That enough to protect
what you want to protect?

238
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:32,137
I'll prove it is.

239
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:35,015
The next time I see my reflection
in Haru's eyes,

240
00:12:35,682 --> 00:12:37,517
<i>I wanna see a wolf I respect.</i>

241
00:12:39,519 --> 00:12:40,896
If it's for that,

242
00:12:40,979 --> 00:12:42,355
then I can fight.

243
00:12:42,439 --> 00:12:43,815
Come on.

244
00:12:43,899 --> 00:12:46,359
You never change, do you?

245
00:12:47,569 --> 00:12:48,612
Thank you for your help.

246
00:12:49,279 --> 00:12:51,281
{\an8}[grunts] Try not to die.

247
00:12:51,364 --> 00:12:53,867
{\an8}You owe me money for the dental work.

248
00:12:53,950 --> 00:12:55,285
{\an8}[chuckles]

249
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:03,502
[announcer] <i>It's now time
to introduce each of the gangs!</i>

250
00:13:04,461 --> 00:13:07,422
With pride as high as their heels!

251
00:13:07,506 --> 00:13:10,509
The big sisters of the Black Market,
the Inari-Gumi!

252
00:13:10,592 --> 00:13:12,093
[man] Ten!

253
00:13:12,177 --> 00:13:14,930
Now the flashy and extravagant samurai!

254
00:13:15,013 --> 00:13:18,183
Loyalty and brotherhood... The Madara-Gumi!

255
00:13:18,934 --> 00:13:21,686
Covered in scales
as strong as their bonds!

256
00:13:21,770 --> 00:13:24,856
Rugged and independent... the Doku-Gumi!

257
00:13:25,357 --> 00:13:30,028
Next! Will these champions from last year
be able to defend their throne?

258
00:13:30,111 --> 00:13:33,907
The kings of the beasts... Shishi-Gumi!

259
00:13:36,535 --> 00:13:40,747
And for the first time in 30 years,
we have a newcomer!

260
00:13:40,830 --> 00:13:44,000
The gray wolf, Legoshi!

261
00:13:44,751 --> 00:13:47,754
Hey, isn't that wolf wanted for devouring?

262
00:13:47,837 --> 00:13:49,339
With a ten-million bounty.

263
00:13:49,422 --> 00:13:50,549
Let's grab him then!

264
00:13:51,883 --> 00:13:53,385
[announcer] The rules are simple!

265
00:13:53,468 --> 00:13:55,470
We ignite each contestant's blood.

266
00:13:55,554 --> 00:13:59,391
The brightness and shape of the flame,
as well as the strength of the scent,

267
00:13:59,474 --> 00:14:01,184
will decide the winner!

268
00:14:01,268 --> 00:14:06,231
The winner earns the seat of
Black Market leader for one full year.

269
00:14:06,314 --> 00:14:07,482
On top of that,

270
00:14:07,566 --> 00:14:10,485
they will receive this special prize
of meat!

271
00:14:10,569 --> 00:14:11,820
[gasping]

272
00:14:11,903 --> 00:14:14,656
Wow...talk about delicious!

273
00:14:16,157 --> 00:14:17,909
[smirks]

274
00:14:21,663 --> 00:14:23,415
Is everything ready?

275
00:14:23,498 --> 00:14:26,084
Alright then... Ignite!

276
00:14:30,255 --> 00:14:31,506
[crowd cheering]

277
00:14:40,682 --> 00:14:41,808
Gotta be Inari-Gumi.

278
00:14:41,892 --> 00:14:43,268
No, Madara-Gumi for sure.

279
00:14:43,351 --> 00:14:44,269
It's Doku-Gumi!

280
00:14:44,352 --> 00:14:47,188
Shishi-Gumi's scent
is kind of weak this year.

281
00:14:47,272 --> 00:14:48,523
[Ten chuckles]

282
00:14:48,607 --> 00:14:51,401
Look at you lions
breaking new ground by putting

283
00:14:51,484 --> 00:14:54,195
an herbivore of all things on the throne,

284
00:14:54,279 --> 00:14:56,573
but it seems
you've gotten a little soft this year.

285
00:14:56,656 --> 00:14:59,451
Ahh!
I don't believe I've introduced myself.

286
00:14:59,534 --> 00:15:01,119
[hissing] How rude of me.

287
00:15:01,202 --> 00:15:04,831
My name is Melon
and I'm the new boss of the Shishi-Gumi.

288
00:15:04,915 --> 00:15:07,083
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

289
00:15:07,167 --> 00:15:09,711
So I guess you ended up
with the short straw, huh?

290
00:15:09,794 --> 00:15:11,838
Shishi-Gumi's time is over.

291
00:15:11,922 --> 00:15:12,964
Really?

292
00:15:13,506 --> 00:15:14,716
Watch yourself.

293
00:15:14,799 --> 00:15:17,552
Underestimating us
isn't the smartest move.

294
00:15:17,636 --> 00:15:19,512
That would be a fatal mistake.

295
00:15:19,596 --> 00:15:21,556
[laughing]

296
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:23,099
Consider yourself warned!

297
00:15:23,183 --> 00:15:24,643
[sniff] Ahh...

298
00:15:24,726 --> 00:15:28,438
the truth is, Shishi-Gumi's scent
is pathetically weak.

299
00:15:28,521 --> 00:15:29,522
I must admit.

300
00:15:30,315 --> 00:15:31,816
Guess I'll add to it.

301
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:34,819
- [grunts]
- [groans]

302
00:15:35,987 --> 00:15:36,947
Agata, no!

303
00:15:37,739 --> 00:15:38,907
Agata!

304
00:15:38,990 --> 00:15:40,617
You crazy bastard!

305
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:41,660
How could you?

306
00:15:42,327 --> 00:15:43,578
[Jimma gasps]

307
00:15:44,788 --> 00:15:45,664
Boss...

308
00:15:46,498 --> 00:15:48,249
This will give us

309
00:15:48,333 --> 00:15:49,876
the strongest scent, right?

310
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:51,920
- [male] Shishi-Gumi!
- Yeah.

311
00:15:55,632 --> 00:15:57,258
What do you think you're doing?

312
00:15:57,342 --> 00:15:58,760
That's against the rules!

313
00:15:58,843 --> 00:15:59,761
[grunts]

314
00:15:59,844 --> 00:16:03,348
The nonsense of these silly turf wars
should be against the rules!

315
00:16:03,932 --> 00:16:06,226
We love blood, and meat,

316
00:16:06,309 --> 00:16:07,936
let's celebrate it!

317
00:16:08,019 --> 00:16:09,854
You all want meat, right?

318
00:16:09,938 --> 00:16:12,190
You want to eat the meat, sure!

319
00:16:12,273 --> 00:16:15,402
So then why would you settle
for just the smell!?

320
00:16:15,485 --> 00:16:17,862
Come on, wake up already!

321
00:16:17,946 --> 00:16:21,116
- That's right!
- Today is Meat Appreciation Day!

322
00:16:21,199 --> 00:16:22,409
[groans]

323
00:16:22,492 --> 00:16:24,995
You all love meat, don't you?

324
00:16:25,078 --> 00:16:27,622
That's why you're here
in the Black Market!

325
00:16:27,706 --> 00:16:29,541
Damn straight! Yeah!

326
00:16:29,624 --> 00:16:30,917
[Melon laughing maniacally]

327
00:16:31,001 --> 00:16:34,671
What kind of beast are you
if you don't embrace your instincts?

328
00:16:34,754 --> 00:16:37,173
Accept the thing you love,

329
00:16:37,257 --> 00:16:39,342
Black Market!

330
00:16:39,426 --> 00:16:42,137
Rule violation! Restrain him!

331
00:16:44,222 --> 00:16:45,849
[commotion]

332
00:16:53,648 --> 00:16:54,941
I think I get it...

333
00:16:55,025 --> 00:16:56,234
Anything goes tonight.

334
00:16:56,735 --> 00:16:59,696
I'll let loose a little bit.
What do ya say?

335
00:16:59,779 --> 00:17:01,614
This gets my blood pumping!

336
00:17:02,157 --> 00:17:03,825
Legoshi,

337
00:17:03,908 --> 00:17:06,161
this will be your final night.

338
00:17:06,244 --> 00:17:10,165
Why not make it spectacular?
[laughing maniacally]

339
00:17:13,668 --> 00:17:16,671
It's nice, but weren't there more
dinosaurs last year?

340
00:17:16,755 --> 00:17:18,715
The ones Cherryton School makes.

341
00:17:18,798 --> 00:17:21,342
[female] I heard that school's
had a lot of trouble lately.

342
00:17:21,426 --> 00:17:23,553
- Huh, like what?
- I don't really know the details...

343
00:17:24,304 --> 00:17:26,890
This is my first time at a land festival.

344
00:17:26,973 --> 00:17:31,186
[Seven] Surely Legoshi wouldn't show up
at a place this crowded, right?

345
00:17:31,269 --> 00:17:33,688
Maybe, but we made a promise,

346
00:17:33,772 --> 00:17:36,649
that he and I
would light a candle here together.

347
00:17:37,275 --> 00:17:39,903
Well, he strikes me as a kid
that keeps promises.

348
00:17:39,986 --> 00:17:42,405
Hey, which direction is the wind blowing?

349
00:17:42,489 --> 00:17:43,490
[licks]

350
00:17:43,573 --> 00:17:44,699
[sniffs]

351
00:17:46,076 --> 00:17:47,702
Hmm, it's blowing in from the ocean.

352
00:17:47,786 --> 00:17:49,746
[groans] Mind if we move upwind?

353
00:17:49,829 --> 00:17:52,040
So Legoshi can find me by my scent.

354
00:17:53,792 --> 00:17:56,336
She can be pretty assertive, huh?

355
00:17:56,419 --> 00:17:58,338
Land creatures have legs

356
00:17:58,421 --> 00:18:00,548
that they use to walk on the ground.

357
00:18:00,632 --> 00:18:02,801
The way someone walks reveals their heart.

358
00:18:03,468 --> 00:18:05,553
And I definitely know how she feels...

359
00:18:06,429 --> 00:18:07,597
She's in love.

360
00:18:09,516 --> 00:18:11,851
[Mayor] And also, switch these two.

361
00:18:11,935 --> 00:18:13,353
I'll get right on it, sir.

362
00:18:13,436 --> 00:18:14,813
[announcer] <i>Everyone!</i>

363
00:18:14,896 --> 00:18:18,441
<i>This year's Festival of the Meteor
is finally here!</i>

364
00:18:18,525 --> 00:18:19,818
[announcement continues]

365
00:18:19,901 --> 00:18:21,861
FESTIVAL OF THE METEOR TIME SCHEDULE

366
00:18:21,945 --> 00:18:23,947
3. SURPRISE ANNOUNCEMENT (FOOD)

367
00:18:25,490 --> 00:18:29,119
<i>I guess they're about to announce
the news about lab-grown meat.</i>

368
00:18:29,202 --> 00:18:30,203
[sighs]

369
00:18:30,703 --> 00:18:33,248
Louis, it's up to you, buddy.

370
00:18:33,331 --> 00:18:34,541
We're counting on you.

371
00:18:35,125 --> 00:18:36,417
{\an8}Just leave it to me.

372
00:18:39,629 --> 00:18:41,381
Oh no, I think it's starting!

373
00:18:41,464 --> 00:18:43,133
Hurry, aren't you done?

374
00:18:43,883 --> 00:18:46,094
[grunts] Lift it up a little higher.

375
00:18:46,177 --> 00:18:47,512
[straining]

376
00:18:47,595 --> 00:18:49,055
[Fudge] A little higher!

377
00:18:49,139 --> 00:18:50,181
[gasps]

378
00:18:50,265 --> 00:18:52,225
Okay! We're good!

379
00:18:52,308 --> 00:18:53,226
Put it down.

380
00:18:54,853 --> 00:18:56,146
Huh?

381
00:18:56,229 --> 00:18:58,106
[Sanu] Good work everybody.

382
00:18:58,773 --> 00:18:59,983
[all] Sanu!

383
00:19:00,525 --> 00:19:02,402
[Sanu] Anything else we need to do?

384
00:19:02,485 --> 00:19:05,238
- Has the tech crew checked lighting?
- I'll flip the breaker!

385
00:19:05,321 --> 00:19:06,865
- Makeup?
- We're about to start.

386
00:19:06,948 --> 00:19:09,075
[Sheila] Leave it to me.
Are the tools over there?

387
00:19:09,159 --> 00:19:10,410
Yes, over there!

388
00:19:11,286 --> 00:19:12,662
[panting]

389
00:19:12,745 --> 00:19:14,706
Has anyone seen where Pina's at?

390
00:19:14,789 --> 00:19:17,125
Isn't he hanging out with girls
from the other schools?

391
00:19:19,043 --> 00:19:19,919
[Miguno] Jeez!

392
00:19:20,003 --> 00:19:23,214
You took forever to fix your ear fur.
That's why we're late.

393
00:19:23,298 --> 00:19:26,259
Of course I did!
Gotta look good for the ladies!

394
00:19:26,342 --> 00:19:28,761
Y'all hungry? I already made a menu!

395
00:19:28,845 --> 00:19:31,222
How much are you gonna eat, bro?

396
00:19:31,306 --> 00:19:33,057
[Miguno] I can't wait! I covered a band

397
00:19:33,141 --> 00:19:35,685
at last year's school festival
that's playing tonight!

398
00:19:35,768 --> 00:19:38,479
[Kolo] Heck yeah! Jack are you ready to--

399
00:19:39,189 --> 00:19:40,523
WANTED: - CHARGE: MURDER

400
00:19:40,607 --> 00:19:42,108
[sighs softly]

401
00:19:42,192 --> 00:19:43,568
[all gasp]

402
00:19:44,194 --> 00:19:47,030
[panting]

403
00:19:47,113 --> 00:19:48,156
[Legoshi] This is crazy!

404
00:19:49,949 --> 00:19:51,326
[screams]

405
00:19:51,910 --> 00:19:53,494
You're not getting away!

406
00:19:54,078 --> 00:19:55,705
[groans]

407
00:19:55,788 --> 00:19:57,081
{\an8}Oh, Grandpa...

408
00:19:57,749 --> 00:20:00,043
Who do you think you're calling "Grandpa"?

409
00:20:00,793 --> 00:20:02,629
[both grunting]

410
00:20:03,379 --> 00:20:06,591
[Savon] Komodo dragon venom
doesn't do it for ya, huh?

411
00:20:07,550 --> 00:20:09,552
Fists and tail it is, then.

412
00:20:09,636 --> 00:20:10,887
Little boy.

413
00:20:10,970 --> 00:20:13,014
[gasps] Beautiful...

414
00:20:14,057 --> 00:20:17,185
<i>I feel so safe...
like being hugged by Grandpa.</i>

415
00:20:20,730 --> 00:20:22,565
[thud, groans]

416
00:20:23,900 --> 00:20:26,152
[Savon chuckles]

417
00:20:26,236 --> 00:20:29,822
Come on, kid,
I hope this isn't you putting up a fight.

418
00:20:29,906 --> 00:20:30,865
[spits]

419
00:20:32,909 --> 00:20:36,246
[whimpering]

420
00:20:39,707 --> 00:20:41,000
[commotion]

421
00:20:41,084 --> 00:20:42,001
I'm outta here!

422
00:20:42,669 --> 00:20:45,004
[thud, groans]

423
00:20:45,755 --> 00:20:47,382
- [grunts]
- [screams]

424
00:20:50,927 --> 00:20:52,095
We can't fight in here!

425
00:20:52,178 --> 00:20:53,346
We'll both be crushed!

426
00:20:53,429 --> 00:20:55,807
[Savon chuckles] Worry about yourself!

427
00:20:55,890 --> 00:20:57,850
- [grunts]
- [groans]

428
00:20:57,934 --> 00:21:00,603
What's a fight without a little danger?

429
00:21:01,104 --> 00:21:03,147
If you fight, expect to get hurt,

430
00:21:03,231 --> 00:21:05,566
expect pain and-- [gasps]

431
00:21:05,650 --> 00:21:07,318
[groaning]

432
00:21:08,569 --> 00:21:10,571
The more wounded a creature gets,

433
00:21:11,072 --> 00:21:13,491
the more beautiful that creature becomes!

434
00:21:14,158 --> 00:21:15,952
[both grunt softly]

435
00:21:18,788 --> 00:21:21,541
[sighs] Maybe our values are kind of...

436
00:21:22,292 --> 00:21:24,836
- kind of similar in a way?
- [Savon grunts]

437
00:21:25,753 --> 00:21:27,463
You and me ain't done.

438
00:21:27,547 --> 00:21:30,842
Our spirits are a lot stronger
than this crumbling rock.

439
00:21:31,384 --> 00:21:32,260
Take this.

440
00:21:32,343 --> 00:21:33,928
Whoa.

441
00:21:34,012 --> 00:21:35,888
Woah, it's wiggling around!

442
00:21:35,972 --> 00:21:38,725
It's freshly severed,
so it's still got some life.

443
00:21:38,808 --> 00:21:40,935
This is a message from the Doku-Gumi.

444
00:21:41,019 --> 00:21:42,854
- You're welcome, kid.
- Huh?

445
00:21:43,438 --> 00:21:44,605
This is a message?

446
00:21:45,523 --> 00:21:47,275
"The beasts of the Black Market...

447
00:21:47,358 --> 00:21:49,902
don't deserve such an easy heart."

448
00:21:49,986 --> 00:21:50,945
Huh?

449
00:21:52,572 --> 00:21:54,282
- [beeping]
- [gasps]

450
00:21:55,491 --> 00:21:57,201
[groans]

451
00:22:01,289 --> 00:22:03,458
[closing tune playing]
